  "level_shipped": "L1r",
  "level_name": "Conversion ratio (fallback)",
  "shipping_reason": "Shipping rule: no model passes the held-out checks here (C3 and C3r: in 2018-2019 Aqua saw 16 to 21 percent more than any harmonized version), so the conversion-ratio fallback ships, with one constant per calendar month. The detection curve passes C0, C1, C1b, C2, C4 and C8; the fallback fails C2 (-0.119), C3 (0.288) and C3r (-0.196). Region added after the start (decision 36); not pre-registered.",
  "unit": "Aqua-equivalent fire cells",
  "unit_note": "One fire cell is a 1 km square (0.01 degree) with fire in one satellite pass. Before February 2012: what Aqua MODIS reported. From February 2012: what Aqua would have reported, computed from VIIRS with a conversion ratio, scaled by a constant fitted for each calendar month because the two sensors' relation follows the season.",
